From cd5f2d0262f793ca26f65f01f9cafa0b2326b530 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:45:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0199 -- the audio cost diagnostics time their
 calls only when SDL_HINT_DOS_AUDIO_DIAG_TIMING is set

Why: the temporary S7 cost diagnostics (SDL/0141's OPL3 register write, SDL/0146-0147's GUS state, voice
and upload brackets) read uclock() twice per call in every build, whether or not anything consumes the
result. On the 486 that is PIT reads on the hottest audio paths: two per OPL3 register write, and the
write can run from the IRQ-0 music pump. Their only consumer is dosags' AUDIOPRB summary (ags 0059 and
its extensions), and no current gate or scorer reads that summary.

What: SDL_DOSAudioDiagTiming() (core/dos/SDL_dos.h) latches SDL_HINT_DOS_AUDIO_DIAG_TIMING, default
false, on its first call. Each diagnostic site reads the clock and records its sample only when it is on;
the hardware writes themselves are unchanged. The first call must be on the main thread, since it reads a
hint; dosags' engine makes it at audio init, before any ISR is hooked. With the hint set, every site
behaves exactly as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
